BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 678 Tm (1. Confirm journal UUID, sequence ordering and transaction boundaries before recovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 661.5 Tm (Journal records from a different volume must never be replayed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 635 Tm (2. Account for revoke records so stale logged blocks are not restored over newer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 618.5 Tm (transactions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 592 Tm (3. Respect the distinct guarantees of journalling modes: metadata consistency is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 575.5 Tm (equivalent to durable contents for every recently written file.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 549 Tm (4. Verify that replayed metadata remains within filesystem and block-group bounds and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 532.5 Tm (that the resulting inode, bitmap and directory state is coherent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 506 Tm (5. Do not interpret every ext3 volume as ext2 simply because the basic inode layout looks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 489.5 Tm (familiar; an outstanding recovery flag matters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 463 Tm (6. After replay, check incompatible and read-only feature masks before writable access,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 446.5 Tm (particularly when using a driver from a different era.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 55 420 Tm (7. Preserve the journal and the original image when an unclean shutdown is suspected;) Tj ET
